{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"13":{"eng-name":"The Chapters on Rulings","ara-name":"كتاب الأحكام"}},"section_detail":{"13":{"hadithnumber_first":2308,"hadithnumber_last":2374,"arabicnumber_first":2308,"arabicnumber_last":2374}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2353,"arabicnumber":2353,"text":"Rapporté par Kathir bin 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin 'Awf : J’ai entendu le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ) dire : “Il est permis de réconcilier des musulmans, sauf si la réconciliation interdit ce qui est permis ou autorise ce qui est interdit.”","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}],"reference":{"book":13,"hadith":46},"chapter":{"id":23,"ara-name":"باب الصُّلْحِ","eng-name":"Reconciliation","isFirstHadith":true}}]}